OL,3,GNEWSAVolunteer-run railway future
OL,4,Asecured with lease
OL,5,
OL,6,FRailway enthusiasts have been granted a
OL,7,F25-year lease to continue the
OL,8,Frestoration of a track.
OL,10,FThe group took over Woodhorn Narrow
OL,11,FGauge Railway, in Ashington, in 2024
OL,12,Fand had asked Northumberland County
OL,13,FCouncil for a workable lease so they
OL,14,Fcould officially submit funding
OL,15,Fapplications and ease the financial
OL,16,Fchallenges of the modernising work.
OL,18,FGroup member, Christine Heath said the
OL,19,Fwork was almost complete and she hoped
OL,20,Fthe railway can open to the public
OL,21,Faround Easter 2027.
OL,23,APub: 09-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
